  "id": "Compound::DB00748 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Carbinoxamine is shown to bind to Cyp2e1 and Cyp2d6, both of which are involved in the oxidation of arachidonic acid. This binding leads to the participation of these enzymes in the arachidonic acid epoxygenase and monooxygenase activities, which ultimately result in the participation of Cyp2b6. The shared pathway through these enzymes suggests a potential mechanism by which Carbinoxamine may influence Cyp2b6 activity. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a robust relationship between Carbinoxamine and Cyp2b6 through a common intermediate, Cyp2e1 and Cyp2d6. The mechanism involves the inhibition of arachidonic acid metabolism, which could have implications for the regulation of lipid mediators and their physiological effects. The integration of these pathways supports a mechanistic link between Carbinoxamine and Cyp2b6, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct effect on Cyp2b6.",
